309955db27a docs(security): say the cache's Set-Cookie rule has no effect on Flutter web (#1010)
lib/core/network/interceptors/cache_interceptor.dart:85:/// The `Set-Cookie` rule has **no effect on Flutter web**. Browsers never
docs/api/core/network.md:866:- The **response** carries no `Cache-Control` `no-store`, `private` or `no-cache` directive, no `Pragma: no-cache` and no `Set-Cookie`. The first two mark a body the server does not want in a shared or persistent cache - an anonymous email-verification or password-reset check, a presigned download. `no-cache` allows storage only with revalidation on every reuse, which this cache does not do. Such a response is passed through without being written, and any entry already stored for that URL is removed. **On Flutter web the `Set-Cookie` rule never fires:** browsers hide `Set-Cookie` from script (a forbidden response header in the Fetch spec), and dio's web adapter only sees what `getAllResponseHeaders()` returns. A web build relies on the server sending `Cache-Control: private` or `no-store` for a cookie-setting response.
